/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Callback Callback
 * @ingroup Foundation_Functional
 *
 * @brief Generic callback wrapper for free functions and member functions.
 *
 * Callback provides a lightweight mechanism for storing and invoking
 * callable targets without requiring dynamic memory allocation.
 *
 * Supported callable types:
 *
 * - Free functions.
 * - Static member functions.
 * - Non-static member functions.
 *
 * The implementation is intended for embedded and desktop applications
 * where deterministic memory usage is important.
 *
 * @section FoundationCallbackOverview Overview
 *
 * A Callback object can be in one of three states:
 *
 * - Unbound.
 * - Bound to a free function.
 * - Bound to a member function and object instance.
 *
 * Invocation is performed through a common interface:
 *
 * @code
 * callback.invoke(...);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationCallbackFreeFunctions Free Functions
 *
 * Binding a free function:
 *
 * @code
 * void OnMessage(uint8_t value)
 * {
 * }
 *
 * Foundation::Functional::Callback<void, uint8_t> callback;
 *
 * callback.bind(OnMessage);
 *
 * callback.invoke(42);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationCallbackMemberFunctions Member Functions
 *
 * Binding a non-static member function:
 *
 * @code
 * class Printer {
 * public:
 *
 *     void Print(uint8_t value)
 *     {
 *     }
 * };
 *
 * Printer printer;
 *
 * Foundation::Functional::Callback<void, uint8_t> callback;
 *
 * callback.bind<
 *     Printer,
 *     &Printer::Print
 * >(&printer);
 *
 * callback.invoke(42);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationCallbackReturnValues Return Values
 *
 * Callbacks may return values:
 *
 * @code
 * int Add(
 *     int a,
 *     int b
 * ) {
 *     return a + b;
 * }
 *
 * Foundation::Functional::Callback<int, int, int> callback;
 *
 * callback.bind(Add);
 *
 * int result = callback.invoke(2, 3);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationCallbackVoidSpecializations Void Specializations
 *
 * The library provides internal specializations for:
 *
 * - Callback<R, void>
 * - Callback<void, Args...>
 * - Callback<void, void>
 *
 * These specializations reduce implementation complexity and avoid
 * unnecessary argument handling when no parameters or return values
 * are required.
 *
 * @section FoundationCallbackEmbedded Embedded Usage
 *
 * Callback is designed to:
 *
 * - Avoid heap allocation.
 * - Avoid RTTI.
 * - Avoid virtual dispatch.
 * - Work on resource-constrained microcontrollers.
 *
 * Typical applications include:
 *
 * - Event systems.
 * - State machines.
 * - MIDI message handlers.
 * - Interrupt dispatchers.
 * - Task schedulers.
 * - Hardware abstraction layers.
 *
 * @section FoundationCallbackRelated Related Components
 *
 * Callback is commonly used by:
 *
 * - Message parsers.
 * - Event dispatchers.
 * - Scheduling systems.
 * - Driver callbacks.
 *
 * @see Foundation::Functional::Callback
 */